Article 11
(1) The Focal Point for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection encourages the implementation of the selection and designation of a Focal Point in each PD; in each PD, the Focal Point consists of officials and/or staff who handle planning and/or program duties.
(2) The Focal Point for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) has the following duties:
 a. promoting Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the work unit;
 b. facilitating the preparation of PD work plans and budgeting that are responsive to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
 c. conducting training, outreach/socialization, and advocacy on Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to all officials and staff within the PD environment;
 d. reporting the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to the leadership of the PD;
 e. encouraging the implementation of analysis of the Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Budget; and
 f. facilitating the preparation of data on Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in each PD.
(3) The Focal Point for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) is selected and designated by the leadership of the PD.

