Part Three
Formation of the Working Group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City

Article
(1) In an effort to accelerate the institutionalization of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in all PD, a working group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City is formed.
(2) Members of the working group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection are all heads/leaders of PD.
(3) The Mayor appoints the Head of PD whose duties cover Women's Empowerment as Chair of the Working Group and Head of the Secretariat of the Regional Working Group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
(4) The formation of the City Working Group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection is established by Mayor's Decree.

Article
The City Working Group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as referred to in Article has the duties:
a. to promote and facilitate Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to each PD;
b. to implement socialization and advocacy of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to sub-district heads, Village Heads and Village Chiefs;
c. to prepare work programs every year;
d. to encourage the realization of planning and budgeting that is Responsive to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
e. to prepare the work plan of the working group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection every year;
f. to be responsible to the Mayor through the Deputy Mayor, to formulate policy recommendations to the Mayor;
g. to prepare a regional profile of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
i. to monitor the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in each agency;
j. to establish a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;
k. to prepare a regional action plan for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the City; and
l. to encourage the implementation of selection and appointment of Focal Points in each PD.

